# Fantasy Refresh — Multi-League Data Architecture
*Designed May 2026*

---

## Design Principles

1. **League isolation** — all game data scoped under /leagues/{leagueId}/
2. **Shared globals** — player pool, user profiles live outside leagues
3. **Backward compatible** — 2026 legacy paths migrated cleanly
4. **Scalable** — same structure works for 1 league or 10,000
5. **Simple Firebase rules** — leagueId in path enables clean security rules

---

## ID Strategy

| Entity | Format | Example | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| League | `fr_` + 8 random alphanum | `fr_a8x3k2p9` | Auto-generated at creation |
| User | Firebase Auth UID | `abc123xyz` | Already in use |
| Season | 4-digit year | `2026` | |
| Week | Integer | `1`-`18` | |
| Game | Tank01 format | `20260909_NE@SEA` | |

